================================================================================
Academic attribution (papers and data)
================================================================================

The following external scientific works are referenced or used as benchmarks
within this project. Their copyright remains with the original authors/publishers;
this listing is for attribution only and does not imply any license grant.

  Evenbly & Vidal (2009)
    "Algorithms for entanglement renormalization"
    Physical Review B 79, 144108. DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevB.79.144108
    Used as : the binary-MERA construction followed in the implementation.
    Preprint: https://arxiv.org/abs/0707.1454

  Evenbly & Vidal (2011)
    "Tensor network states and geometry"
    Physical Review Letters 107, 010501. DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevLett.107.010501
    Used as : the structural property (geometry predetermined) invoked in the
              L5 honest-boundary discussion.
    Preprint: https://arxiv.org/abs/1106.1082

  Evenbly & Vidal (2015)
    "Tensor network renormalization"
    Physical Review Letters 115, 180405. DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevLett.115.180405
    Preprint: https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.0732

  Swingle (2012)
    "Entanglement renormalization and holography"
    Physical Review D 86, 065007. DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevD.86.065007
    Used as : background motivation for the entanglement-renormalization /
              emergent-spacetime discussion.
    Preprint: https://arxiv.org/abs/0905.1317

  Calabrese & Cardy (2004)
    "Entanglement entropy and quantum field theory"
    Journal of Statistical Mechanics, P06002. DOI: 10.1088/1742-5468/2004/06/P06002
    Used as : the parameter-free CFT finite-size formula that anchors the
              external validation in the companion manuscript.
    Preprint: https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0405152

  Vidal (2007)
    "Entanglement Renormalization"
    Physical Review Letters 99, 220405. DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevLett.99.220405
    Preprint: https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/0512165

